  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_007: RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA, acc≈0.485), so evidence is extremely sparse and the most critical uncertainty is whether adding the image modality provides any signal at all. config_009 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, no aggregation, concat fusion) is the minimal, clean extension of config_007: it keeps the RNA side identical (same encoder, same profile setting) and adds only a simple ResNet50 image branch with basic concatenation. This isolates the effect of image information without confounding changes to the RNA encoder, profile count, aggregation, or fusion complexity. If accuracy improves, it validates the multimodal premise and justifies investing further in image encoders and fusion strategies; if it does not, it redirects the budget toward RNA representation (scgpt/scvi) or multiprofile aggregation. Under a limited budget, resolving this core question before exploring more complex multimodal or learned-encoder configurations is the highest-information next step."
}

